Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ContentOS does not vendor its dependencies; they are resolved from the npm
registry at install time and each keeps its own license. The dependency tree is
predominantly MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC and BSD. Notable exceptions worth calling out:

  * lightningcss, lightningcss-win32-x64-msvc — Mozilla Public License 2.0
    Source: https://github.com/parcel-bundler/lightningcss
    Reached transitively through Tailwind CSS. MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft:
    modifications to those files must be shared, but linking them from
    Apache-2.0 code imposes no obligation on this project's source.

  * axe-core — Mozilla Public License 2.0
    Source: https://github.com/dequelabs/axe-core
    Reached transitively; development/testing only.

  * @img/sharp-* — Apache-2.0, with prebuilt binaries that dynamically link
    libvips and its LGPL-3.0-or-later dependencies.
    Source: https://github.com/lovell/sharp
    Dynamic linking, which is what the LGPL permits without relicensing.

To review the licenses actually resolved for your install:

    pnpm licenses list

